\section definition_mfcc Mel-Frequency Cepstral Coefficients

xtract_mfcc()

\f[ c_i = \sum_{m=1}^{M} \ln \max\left(E_m, \epsilon \max_j E_j\right) \cos\left(\frac{\pi i (m - \tfrac{1}{2})}{M}\right) \text{ when } \max_j E_j > 0, \text{ and } c_i = 0 \text{ otherwise}, \quad i = 0, \dots, M-1, \quad E_m = \sum_k H_m(k) P_k, \quad \epsilon = 2^{-52} \f]

Sources:
- Origin: Davis and Mermelstein (1980). "Comparison of parametric representations for monosyllabic word recognition in continuously spoken sentences". IEEE Transactions on Acoustics, Speech, and Signal Processing 28(4), equation 1 and figure 1. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/TASSP.1980.1163420">doi:10.1109/TASSP.1980.1163420</a>
- Formulation: Rabiner and Juang (1993). "Fundamentals of speech recognition". PTR Prentice Hall, section 4.5.6, equation 4.90
- Formulation: Young, Evermann, Gales, Hain, Kershaw, Liu, Moore, Odell, Ollason, Povey, Valtchev and Woodland (2009). "The HTK book, for HTK version 3.4". Cambridge University Engineering Department, section 5.4, equation 5.13

Validation level 0, not checked.

\section definition_dct Discrete Cosine Transform

xtract_dct()

No published source is listed.

Validation level 0, not checked.

\section definition_harmonic_spectrum Harmonic Spectrum

xtract_harmonic_spectrum()

No published source is listed.

Validation level 0, not checked.

\section definition_lpc Linear predictive coding coefficients

xtract_lpc()

\f[ E_0 = r_0, \quad k_i = -\frac{r_i + \sum_{j=1}^{i-1} a_j^{(i-1)} r_{i-j}}{E_{i-1}}, \quad a_i^{(i)} = k_i, \quad a_j^{(i)} = a_j^{(i-1)} + k_i a_{i-j}^{(i-1)}, \quad E_i = (1 - k_i^2) E_{i-1}, \quad i = 1, \dots, p, \quad A(z) = 1 + \sum_{j=1}^{p} a_j^{(p)} z^{-j} \f]

Sources:
- Origin: Atal and Hanauer (1971). "Speech analysis and synthesis by linear prediction of the speech wave". Journal of the Acoustical Society of America 50(2B), appendix E, equations E8 to E10, with the opposite sign. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1121/1.1912679">doi:10.1121/1.1912679</a>
- Formulation: Makhoul (1975). "Linear prediction: a tutorial review". Proceedings of the IEEE 63(4), equations 12 and 38a to 38e. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/PROC.1975.9792">doi:10.1109/PROC.1975.9792</a>

Validation level 0, not checked.

\section definition_lpcc Linear predictive coding cepstral coefficients

xtract_lpcc()

\f[ c_n = -a_n - \frac{1}{n} \sum_{k=\max(1, n-p)}^{n-1} k \, c_k \, a_{n-k}, \quad n = 1, \dots, Q, \quad a_n = 0 \text{ for } n > p \f]

Sources:
- Origin: Atal (1974). "Effectiveness of linear prediction characteristics of the speech wave for automatic speaker identification and verification". Journal of the Acoustical Society of America 55(6), equation 15, in the opposite sign. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1121/1.1914702">doi:10.1121/1.1914702</a>
- Formulation: Rabiner and Juang (1993). "Fundamentals of speech recognition". PTR Prentice Hall, equation 4.19, p. 163, and equation 3.83c, p. 115

Validation level 0, not checked.

